---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>hookwarden — find and fix webhook signature-verification bugs</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Local. Deterministic. Zero-network. Find every webhook-verification bug in JS/TS, Python, and PHP — and apply the fix on the safe subset — in under five minutes."
    />
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-bg text-text">
    <header class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-12">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">hookwarden</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-text/80">
        The only scanner laser-focused on webhook signature verification.
      </p>
    </header>

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-24">
      <section class="rounded-2xl bg-surface p-8">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Find every bug.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text/80">
          Three-state verdicts (<code class="font-mono">verified</code> /
          <code class="font-mono">not-verified</code> /
          <code class="font-mono">manual-review</code>) across JS/TS, Python, and PHP.
          Stripe, GitHub, Shopify, Twilio, Slack, Square. SARIF 2.1.0 output for
          GitHub Code Scanning. Zero network. Zero telemetry.
        </p>
        <pre
          class="mt-6 rounded bg-bg p-4 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>npx hookwarden scan ./your-app</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl bg-surface p-8">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold">
          <span class="text-accent">v0.5 —</span> Apply every safe fix.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text/80">
          hookwarden doesn't just tell you the fix — it applies it. The
          <code class="font-mono">fix</code> subcommand mechanically rewrites the
          <code class="font-mono">safety: safe</code> subset of findings across
          all 3 v1 languages. Dry-run is the default; <code class="font-mono">--write</code>
          opt-in stages atomically and re-scans before commit.
        </p>
        <pre
          class="mt-6 rounded bg-bg p-4 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code># Dry-run (default) — prints unified diff
npx hookwarden fix ./your-app

# Apply via atomic-staging path
npx hookwarden fix ./your-app --write</code></pre>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-text/80">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Three safety modes.</strong>
            <code class="font-mono">--mode safe</code> (default),
            <code class="font-mono">--mode all</code> (refuses in CI without
            <code class="font-mono">--accept-unsafe</code>),
            <code class="font-mono">--mode manual-only-explain</code> for the
            prose-only rules.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Atomic staging.</strong> Rewrites land in
            <code class="font-mono">.hookwarden-fix-staging/&lt;run-id&gt;/</code>;
            re-scan verifies zero new findings before the atomic rename. Failure
            preserves staging for inspection.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Forbidden-range mask.</strong> Never edits
            inside template literals, triple-quoted strings, heredocs, or
            comments.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Versioned JSON schema.</strong>
            <code class="font-mono">--format json</code> emits the v1.0 contract
            at <code class="font-mono">hookwarden.dev/schemas/fix-output.v1.json</code>.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6">
          <a
            href="/cli"
            class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent/80"
            >See the full CLI reference →</a
          >
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
